# The coverage ratchet's floor, read by scripts/check-coverage.sh.
#
# The values are the best aggregate the suites have produced, minus half a point of margin for
# instrument noise — a ratchet, not a target. The script fails a run that lands below these and
# nags when a run lands more than a point above, so the floor only moves in one direction.
#
# First measured 2026-09-27 on the wave that introduced the gate (scoverage 2.5.2, Scala 3.9.0,
# 81 instrumented test modules): line-rate 0.78, branch-rate 0.73 on a docker-less machine, where
# the Testcontainers suites skip — CI measures the same or higher, so the floor sits a point under
# the docker-less reading and both directions are safe. Update by editing both numbers in the same
# commit as the change that moved them, and say in that commit message which suites did it.
SCALA_LINE_RATE_MIN=0.77
SCALA_BRANCH_RATE_MIN=0.72
